{"abstract":"Compared to classical ion-selective electrodes (ISEs) with internal reference solutions, potential stability remains one of the greatest challenges for all-solid-state ISEs. In this paper, a highly stable all-solid-state potassium ISE was developed using thin egg-shell hollow carbon nanospheres (ESHCNs) synthesized via one-pot hydrothermal method as an ion-to-electron transducing layer. The electrodes’ properties were examined by means of cyclic voltammetry, electrochemical impedance spectroscopy, and chronopotentiometry, proving the superior hydrophobicity as well as large interfacial capacitance for these ESHCNs. These characteristics effectively prevented the formation of a water layer between the conducting substrate and polymer film, therefore stabilizing their electrode potential. The prepared electrode exhibited good linearity within potassium ion concentration range of 5.0 × 10-6 ∼ 1.0 × 10-2 mol/L, with a Nernst slope of 55.11 ± 1.6 mV/decade and a detection limit of 1.41 × 10-6 mol/L. It showed excellent long-term stability, with only a decrease of 12.02 % in response-slope after over 18 months of use. For quality control in industrial settings, the amount of K+ contents determined in actual cigarette paper using this electrode was consistent with ion chromatography results, demonstrating its potential for rapid, accurate, and reliable on-site K+ detection with promising industrial applications.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Yu, Saibo","Li, Bin","Chen, Pengfei","Lian, Wenliu","Jiang, Lamei","Jin, Yong","Wu, Ling","Xiao, Zhongliang","Yu, Donghong","Cao, Zhong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-814834"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Cao, Zhong","Jin, Yong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Changsha University of Science and Technology","State Tobacco Monopoly Administration, China Tobacco Corporation"],"keyword":["Potassium ion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an all solid state polymeric membrane potassium ion selective electrode with egg shell hollow carbon nanospheres as ion to electron transducing layer","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=105008127044&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-814834","identifier":[{"id":"105008127044","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c162bd6c-54d4-4fe7-8e4a-1c42df8d94fb"],"keyword":["All-solid-state ion-selective electrode","Cigarette paper analysis","Egg-shell hollow carbon nanospheres","Ion-to-electron transducing layer","Potassium ion","Potentiometric sensor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-48A794F7ADAE64CD882817A6EC3224D6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"changsha university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Changsha University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"state tobacco monopoly administration china tobacco corporation","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Tobacco Monopoly Administration, China Tobacco Corporation","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Applied Supramolecular Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Saibo","key":"yusaibopau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Saibo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bin","key":"libinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Bin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengfei","key":"chenpengfeipau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Pengfei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenliu","key":"lianwenliupau","last":"Lian","name":"Lian, Wenliu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lamei","key":"jianglameipau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Lamei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yong","key":"jinyongpau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Yong","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ling","key":"wulingpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Ling","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhongliang","key":"xiaozhongliangpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Zhongliang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Donghong","key":"yudonghongpau","last":"Yu","locid":"9bf68567-02d0-41e9-a849-c0c03bbdfb9d","name":"Yu, Donghong","orcid":"0000-0002-3035-5035","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhong","key":"caozhongpau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Zhong","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.microc.2025.114287","issn":["0026265X","10959149"],"issn_org":["0026265X"],"journal":"Microchemical Journal","paperid":"114287","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Microchemical Journal","volume":"215"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105008127044"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c162bd6c-54d4-4fe7-8e4a-1c42df8d94fb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An all-solid-state polymeric membrane potassium ion-selective electrode with egg-shell hollow carbon nanospheres as ion-to-electron transducing layer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-814834","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Soil microbial communities play a crucial role in the accumulation and stabilization of soil organic carbon (SOC) through complex processes involving plant residue transformation and mineral interactions. These processes are influenced by plant inputs and modulated by soil properties that are mostly determined by the parent material. However, our understanding is limited regarding the manner in which vegetation and parent material affect microbial community structure, necromass accumulation, and their subsequent impact on SOC storage. To bridge this knowledge gap, we conducted an in-depth investigation focusing on the top-down influence of vegetation type and the bottom-up effect of parent material on microbial-mediated carbon transformation across soil profiles in a tropical region. Our study encompassed 42 sites on three parent materials (basalt, granite, and marine sediments) and four vegetation types (rubber, banana, areca plantations and uncultivated grassland). Soil samples were collected at 0–20, 20–40, 40–80, and 80–100 cm depth. Microbial community structure and necromass were quantified using microbial biomarkers of phospholipid fatty acids and amino sugars, respectively. In rubber plantations, we observed a trend toward higher microbial biomass that, though not significant when compared to other vegetation types, transformed to a significantly higher accumulation of microbial necromass. This increase in microbial necromass was linked to the accumulation of SOC facilitated by the presence of clay size minerals in clayey soils developed from basalt. In particular, basaltic soils were dominated by bacteria, which facilitated the accumulation of bacterial necromass that significantly bolstered its contribution to SOC. In contrast, in sandier soils developed from granite and marine sediments, fungal communities and necromass dominated due to the propensity of fungi for coarser soil environments. Overall, the main impact of vegetation on microbial communities and necromass accumulation was primarily demonstrated for the topsoil. Differences in soil texture arising from different parent materials exert significant effects on the fungal-to bacterial-biomass and necromass ratios, consequently influencing the contribution of fungal and bacterial necromass carbon to SOC across soil profiles. Our study underscores the pivotal role of parent material in governing tropical profile-scale soil carbon storage by shaping the structure of microbial communities and influencing the retention of microbial necromass.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Li, Yu Zhu","Bao, Xue Lian","Tang, Shi-Xin","Xiao, Ke-Qing","Ge, Cheng-Jun","Xie, Hong-Tu","He, Hong-Bo","Mueller, Carsten W.","Liang, Chao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739248"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences","CAS - Shenyang Institute of Applied Ecology","Chinese Academy of Geological Sciences","Hainan University","Technical University of Berlin","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Microbial community","Microbial necromass","Soil organic carbon"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toward soil carbon storage the influence of parent material and vegetation on profile scale microbial community structure and necromass accumulation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-739248","identifier":[{"id":"85187959446","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-68ceeea3-52d4-40ac-9af5-292709f8af84"],"keyword":["Microbial community","Microbial necromass","Parent material","Soil organic carbon","Tropical island"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4293F3B82D33EDED89E86D3F29A47DAE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"cas shenyang institute of applied ecology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Shenyang Institute of Applied Ecology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of geological sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Geological Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"cas research center for eco environmental sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"hainan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hainan University","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geography, People and Processes"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"technical university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Berlin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Yu Zhu","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yu Zhu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xue Lian","key":"baopau","last":"Bao","name":"Bao, Xue Lian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Shi-Xin","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Shi-Xin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Ke-Qing","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Ke-Qing","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Cheng-Jun","key":"gepau","last":"Ge","name":"Ge, Cheng-Jun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hong-Tu","key":"xiepau","last":"Xie","name":"Xie, Hong-Tu","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hong-Bo","key":"hepau","last":"He","name":"He, Hong-Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","first":"Carsten W.","key":"muellerpau","last":"Mueller","locid":"138d0a3a-26ec-465d-9bbd-cbdd44e5b589","name":"Mueller, Carsten W.","orcid":"0000-0003-4119-0544","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chao","key":"liangpau","last":"Liang","name":"Liang, Chao","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.soilbio.2024.109399","issn":["00380717","18793428"],"issn_org":["00380717"],"journal":"Soil Biology & Biochemistry","paperid":"109399","status":"p","title":"Soil Biology & Biochemistry","title_org":"Soil Biology and Biochemistry","volume":"193"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85187959446"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-68ceeea3-52d4-40ac-9af5-292709f8af84"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Toward soil carbon storage : The influence of parent material and vegetation on profile-scale microbial community structure and necromass accumulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739248","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Glioblastoma is the most lethal primary brain tumor with glioblastoma stem cells (GSCs) atop a cellular hierarchy. GSCs often reside in a perivascular niche, where they receive maintenance cues from endothelial cells, but the role of heterogeneous endothelial cell populations remains unresolved. Here, we show that lymphatic endothelial-like cells (LECs), while previously unrecognized in brain parenchyma, are present in glioblastomas and promote growth of CCR7-positive GSCs through CCL21 secretion. Disruption of CCL21–CCR7 paracrine communication between LECs and GSCs inhibited GSC proliferation and growth. LEC-derived CCL21 induced KAT5-mediated acetylation of HMGCS1 on K273 in GSCs to enhance HMGCS1 protein stability. HMGCS1 promoted cholesterol synthesis in GSCs, favorable for tumor growth. Expression of the CCL21–CCR7 axis correlated with KAT5 expression and HMGCS1K273 acetylation in glioblastoma specimens, informing patient outcome. Collectively, glioblastomas contain previously unrecognized LECs that promote the molecular crosstalk between endothelial and tumor cells, offering potentially alternative therapeutic strategies.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Zhao, Linjie","Qiu, Zhixin","Yang, Zhengnan","Xu, Lian","Pearce, Thomas M.","Wu, Qiulian","Yang, Kailin","Li, Fu Long","Saulnier, Olivier","Fei, Fan","Yu, Huaxu","Gimple, Ryan C.","Varadharajan, Venkateshwari","Liu, Juxiu","Hendrikse, Liam D.","Fong, Vernon","Wang, Wei","Zhang, Jiao","Lv, Deguan","Lee, Derrick","Lehrich, Brandon M.","Jin, Chunyu","Ouyang, Liang","Dixit, Deobrat","Wu, Haoxing","Wang, Xiang","Sloan, Andrew E.","Wang, Xiuxing","Huan, Tao","Mark Brown, J.","Goldman, Steven A.","Taylor, Michael D.","Zhou, Shengtao","Rich, Jeremy N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811426"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Canada","China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Case Western Reserve University","Cleveland Clinic Foundation","Department of Environment Science and Engineering, Fudan University","Huzhou Maternity & Child Health Care Hospital","Nanjing Medical University","Sichuan University","University of British Columbia","University of California at San Diego","University of Electronic Science and Technology of China","University of Pittsburgh","University of Rochester","University of Toronto"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lymphatic endothelial like cells promote glioblastoma stem cell growth through cytokine driven cholesterol metabolism","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-811426","identifier":[{"id":"38172338","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85181247534","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-efca2bad-6151-4020-a511-1f6e75863033"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF5DB48579EAA6F9EF13C6C3B50FE7E9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of pittsburgh","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Pittsburgh","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california at san diego","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at San Diego","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"department of environment science and engineering fudan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Department of Environment Science and Engineering, Fudan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"cleveland clinic foundation","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cleveland Clinic Foundation","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"ca","key":"university of toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"cn","key":"university of electronic science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Electronic Science and Technology of China","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"ca","key":"university of british columbia","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of British Columbia","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"us","key":"case western reserve university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Case Western Reserve University","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"cn","key":"huzhou maternity child health care hospital","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huzhou Maternity & Child Health Care Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"cn","key":"nanjing medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"12","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Center for Translational Neuromedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"13","country":"us","key":"university of rochester","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Rochester","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Linjie","key":"zhaolinjiepau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Linjie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Zhixin","key":"qiuzhixinpau","last":"Qiu","name":"Qiu, Zhixin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Zhengnan","key":"yangzhengnanpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Zhengnan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Lian","key":"xulianpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Lian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","