enmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-600e735b-de89-407f-9bd9-4ac564e31359"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The enhanced X-ray Timing and Polarimetry mission – eXTP : an update on its scientific cases, mission profile and development status","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-333173","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Parkinson’s disease (PD) is the second most common neurodegenerative disease in middle-aged and elderly populations, whereas there is no cure for PD so far. Novel animal models and medications await development to elucidate the aetiology of PD and attenuate the symptoms, respectively. Methods: A neurotoxin, 1-methyl-4-phenyl-1,2,3,6-tetrahydropyridine (MPTP), was used in the current study to establish a PD pathologic model in silkworms. The time required to complete specific behaviours was recorded. Dopamine content was detected by ultra-performance liquid chromatography (UPLC). The activity of insect tyrosine hydroxylase (TH) was determined using a double-antibody sandwich method. Oxidative stress was assessed by changes in antioxidant enzyme activity and the content of oxidative products. Results: MPTP-treated silkworms were characterized by impaired motor ability, reduced dopamine content, and elevated oxidative stress level. The expression of TH, a dopamine biosynthetic enzyme within dopaminergic neurons in the brain, was significantly reduced, indicating that dopaminergic neurons were damaged. Moreover, MPTP-induced motility impairment and reduced dopamine level in the silkworm PD model could be rescued after feeding a combination of levodopa (L-dopa [LD]) and carbidopa (CD). MPTP-induced oxidative damage was also alleviated, in ways consistent with other PD animal models. Interestingly, administration of Lycium barbarum polysaccharide (LBP) improved the motor ability, dopamine level, and TH activity, and the oxidative damage was concomitantly reduced in the silkworm PD model. Conclusions: This study provides a promising animal model for elucidating the pathogenesis of PD, as well as a relevant preliminary drug screening (e.g., LBP) and evaluation.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Song, Jiangbo","Liu, Lian","Li, Zhiquan","Mao, Ting","Zhang, Jianfei","Zhou, Lei","Chen, Xin","Shang, Yunzhu","Sun, Tao","Luo, Yuxin","Jiang, Yu","Tan, Duan","Tong, Xiaoling","Dai, Fangyin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-401576"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Southwest University"],"keyword":["Animal model","Dopamine","Oxidative stress","Parkinson s disease"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i lycium barbarum i polysaccharide improves dopamine metabolism and symptoms in an mptp induced model of parkinson s disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12916-022-02621-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-401576","identifier":[{"id":"36303171","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9615188","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85140866131","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0da86981-8cce-4b98-9cbc-f30b98ec61fa"],"keyword":["Animal model","Dopamine","Lycium barbarum polysaccharide","Oxidative stress","Parkinson’s disease","Silkworm"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-086479066DA414ED5445E94CD4C680BE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12916-022-02621-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/325336915/s12916_022_02621_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"southwest university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwest University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Molecular Aging Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jiangbo","key":"songpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Jiangbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lian","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Lian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Zhiquan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"57cc7ee6-b959-4889-aa59-a79a64d4fb72","name":"Li, Zhiquan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ting","key":"maopau","last":"Mao","name":"Mao, Ting","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jianfei","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jianfei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lei","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Lei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xin","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Xin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yunzhu","key":"shangpau","last":"Shang","name":"Shang, Yunzhu","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tao","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Tao","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yuxin","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Yuxin","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yu","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Yu","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Duan","key":"tanpau","last":"Tan","name":"Tan, Duan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaoling","key":"tongpau","last":"Tong","name":"Tong, Xiaoling","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fangyin","key":"daipau","last":"Dai","name":"Dai, Fangyin","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36303171"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12916-022-02621-9","issn":["17417015"],"journal":"BMC Medicine","paperid":"412","status":"p","title":"BMC Medicine","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140866131"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0da86981-8cce-4b98-9cbc-f30b98ec61fa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"<i>Lycium barbarum</i> polysaccharide improves dopamine metabolism and symptoms in an MPTP-induced model of Parkinson’s disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-401576","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Abstract: In recent years, stimuli-responsive polymers, a kind of functional material, have drawn increasing attention. In this paper, acrylamide azobenzene was introduced into the molecularly imprinted polymer by copolymerization with acrylic acid in the presence of template molecules methylene blue, crosslinker N,N '‑methylene bisacrylamide, and initiator azobisisobutyronitrile, which makes the imprinting material have the effect of light-operated and further expand the application range of imprinting materials. Detailed studies of the photo-regulated uptake and release process suggested that the binding affinity of imprinted recognition sites in imprinting materials could be changed under the alternating irradiation of ultraviolet and visible light. The adsorption isotherm experiments and adsorption kinetic experiments showed that the adsorption of methylene blue by the imprinted material conforms to the monolayer chemical adsorption and quasi-second-order kinetic model. Additionally, the relevant thermodynamic parameters were calculated. These thermodynamic parameters proved that the adsorption process was spontaneous, endothermic and entropy-increasing.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Baohe Li, Li","Jiang, Lian","Wang, Yurong","Li, Chenran","Yu, Donghong","Wang, Nong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-063501"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Nong","Yu, Donghong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lanzhou Jiaotong University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"construction and properties of new type photo responsive molecular imprinting materials","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85149994726&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Innovation Fund of Small and Medium-sized Enterprises of Gansu Province (Grant no. 1407GCCA013), the Key Technology and Industrial Application Demonstration Project of High Quality and High Purity Nano Calcium Carbonate of Guangxi Province (Grant no. 17202030-2)."],"id":"S01-000.00-063501","identifier":[{"id":"85149994726","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2e646adb-464d-46bf-978d-031408b94047"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FD8DAAAB91458BE5DB141C6287121E5C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"lanzhou jiaotong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Lanzhou Jiaotong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Applied Supramolecular Chemistry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Chemical Science and Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"baohelilipau","last":"Baohe Li","name":"Baohe Li, Li","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lian","key":"jianglianpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Lian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yurong","key":"wangyurongpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yurong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chenran","key":"lichenranpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Chenran","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Donghong","key":"yudonghongpau","last":"Yu","locid":"9bf68567-02d0-41e9-a849-c0c03bbdfb9d","name":"Yu, Donghong","orcid":"0000-0002-3035-5035","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nong","key":"wangnongpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Nong","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1134/s0965545x22700572","issn":["0965545X","15556107"],"issn_org":["0965545X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Polymer Science - Series A","pages":"673-684","publisher":"Pleiades Publishing","status":"p","title":"Polymer Science - Series A","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149994726"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2e646adb-464d-46bf-978d-031408b94047"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Construction and Properties of New-Type Photo-Responsive Molecular Imprinting Materials","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-063501","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The decline in species richness at higher latitudes is among the most fundamental patterns in ecology. Whether changes in species composition across space (beta-diversity) contribute to this gradient of overall species richness (gamma-diversity) remains hotly debated. Previous studies that failed to resolve the issue suffered from a well-known tendency for small samples in areas with high gamma-diversity to have inflated measures of beta-diversity. Here, we provide a novel analytical test, using beta-diversity metrics that correct the gamma-diversity and sampling biases, to compare beta-diversity and species packing across a latitudinal gradient in tree species richness of 21 large forest plots along a large environmental gradient in East Asia. We demonstrate that after accounting for topography and correcting the gamma-diversity bias, tropical forests still have higher beta-diversity than temperate analogues. This suggests that beta-diversity contributes to the latitudinal species richness gradient as a component of gamma-diversity. Moreover, both niche specialization and niche marginality (a measure of niche spacing along an environmental gradient) also increase towards the equator, after controlling for the effect of topographical heterogeneity. This supports the joint importance of tighter species packing and larger niche space in tropical forests while also demonstrating the importance of local processes in controlling beta-diversity.","author_count":45,"contributors":["Cao, Ke","Condit, Richard","Mi, Xiangcheng","Chen, Lei","Ren, Haibao","Xu, Wubing","Burslem, David F.R.P.","Cai, Chunrong","Cao, Min","Chang, Li Wan","Chu, Chengjin","Cui, Fuxin","Du, Hu","Ediriweera, Sisira","Gunatilleke, C. S.V.","Gunatilleke, I. U.A.N.","Hao, Zhanqing","Jin, Guangze","Li, Jinbo","Li, Buhang","Li, Yide","Liu, Yankun","Ni, Hongwei","O'Brien, Michael J.","Qiao, Xiujuan","Shen, Guochun","Tian, Songyan","Wang, Xihua","Xu, Han","Xu, Yaozhan","Yang, Libing","Yap, Sandra L.","Lian, Juyu","Ye, Wanhui","Yu, Mingjian","Su, Sheng Hsin","Chang-Yang, Chia Hao","Guo, Yili","Li, Xiankun","Zeng, Fuping","Zhu, Daoguang","Zhu, Li","Sun, I. Fang","Ma, Keping","Svenning, Jens Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-248939"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Mi, Xiangcheng"],"country":["China","Philippines","Spain","Sri Lanka","Taiwan","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Normal University","CAS - Guangxi Institute of Botany","Chinese Academy of Forestry","Chinese Academy of Sciences","East China Normal University","Field Museum of Natural History","Morton Arboretum","National Dong Hwa University","National Sun Yat-sen University","Northeast Forestry University","Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","Sun Yat-Sen University","Taiwan Forestry Research Institute","Universidad Rey Juan Carlos","University of Aberdeen","University of Peradeniya","University of the Philippines","Uva Wellassa University","Zhejiang University"],"keyword":["Beta diversity","Gamma diversity","Latitude","Sampling bias"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"species packing and the latitudinal gradient in beta diversity","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8059527/pdf/rspb.2020.3045.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-248939","identifier":[{"id":"85104281581","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8059527","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33849320","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d1495558-7dcf-4d3e-86da-a04956616ab3"]