{"abstract":"Pressurized vertical electro-osmotic dewatering (PVEOD) is an emerging mechanical technology for deep dewatering of wastewater sludge. In this study, the influence of main operation variables including sludge dosage, voltage, mechanical pressure on electro-osmotic dewatering was investigated. Response surface method (RSM) was applied to evaluate and optimize the interactive effects of the three major operating variables. The results indicated the optimum conditions to be 2.70 MPa of mechanical pressure, 18.33 V of voltage and 0.0169 kWh/kg water of energy consumption. Layered distribution study was conducted between anode side and cathode side to investigate the vertical changes of moisture content, zeta potential, three-dimensional excitation emission matrix (3D-EEM) spectra of extracellular polymeric substances, the concentration of proteins and polysaccharides. The morphology changes of sludge observed by microscope images unveiled the possible mechanisms of enhancing the sludge dewaterability in the PVEOD process. The electrochemical at electrodes and electro-osmosis are important for interpreting the dryer sludge at anode layer.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zhang, Yu","Lian, Guanghu","Dong, Chunying","Cai, Meiqiang","Song, Zhijun","Shi, Yuejing","Wu, Liguang","Jin, Micong","Wei, Zongsu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-238489"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Cai, Meiqiang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ningbo Municipal Center for Disease Control and Prevention","Zhejiang Gongshang University"],"keyword":["Activated sludge","Dewaterability","Ions","Optimization","Oxidation","Sewage sludge"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimizing and understanding the pressurized vertical electro osmotic dewatering of activated sludge","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85086089961","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-238489","identifier":[{"id":"85086089961","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000552227000008","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-bf4a0ca6-7787-47f0-9cc7-654a3f01d68e"],"keyword":["Activated sludge","DEWATERABILITY","DOSAGES","Electro-Osmotic dewatering","Extracellular polymeric substance (EPS)","IONS","OPTIMIZATION","OXIDATION","SEWAGE-SLUDGE","Sludge properties"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7D78BC261064C0A0B4B32BBD2146D61E"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang gongshang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang Gongshang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"ningbo municipal center for disease control and prevention","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Ningbo Municipal Center for Disease Control and Prevention","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Guanghu","key":"lianpau","last":"Lian","name":"Lian, Guanghu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Chunying","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Chunying","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Meiqiang","key":"caipau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Meiqiang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhijun","key":"songpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Zhijun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuejing","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Yuejing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Liguang","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Liguang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Micong","key":"jinpau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Micong","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zongsu","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","locid":"e187efc6-abcf-468f-92b6-f27824e33e91","name":"Wei, Zongsu","orcid":"0000-0001-8747-2251","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.psep.2020.05.016","issn":["09575820","17443598"],"issn_org":["09575820"],"journal":"Process Safety and Environmental Protection","pages":"392-402","publisher":"Institution of Chemical Engineers","status":"p","title":"Process Safety and Environmental Protection","volume":"140"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086089961"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bf4a0ca6-7787-47f0-9cc7-654a3f01d68e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Optimizing and understanding the pressurized vertical electro-osmotic dewatering of activated sludge","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-238489","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper documents the 16th data release (DR16) from the Sloan Digital Sky Surveys (SDSS), the fourth and penultimate from the fourth phase (SDSS-IV). This is the first release of data from the Southern Hemisphere survey of the Apache Point Observatory Galactic Evolution Experiment 2 (APOGEE-2); new data from APOGEE-2 North are also included. DR16 is also notable as the final data release for the main cosmological program of the Extended Baryon Oscillation Spectroscopic Survey (eBOSS), and all raw and reduced spectra from that project are released here. DR16 also includes all the data from the Time Domain Spectroscopic Survey and new data from the SPectroscopic IDentification of ERosita Survey programs, both of which were co-observed on eBOSS plates. DR16 has no new data from the Mapping Nearby Galaxies at Apache Point Observatory (MaNGA) survey (or the MaNGA Stellar Library \"MaStar\"). We also preview future SDSS-V operations (due to start in 2020), and summarize plans for the final SDSS-IV data release (DR17).","author_count":313,"contributors":["Ahumada, Romina","Prieto, Carlos Allende","Almeida, Andrés","Anders, Friedrich","Anderson, Scott F.","Andrews, Brett H.","Anguiano, Borja","Arcodia, Riccardo","Armengaud, Eric","Aubert, Marie","Avila, Santiago","Avila-Reese, Vladimir","Badenes, Carles","Balland, Christophe","Barger, Kat","Barrera-Ballesteros, Jorge K.","Basu, Sarbani","Bautista, Julian","Beaton, Rachael L.","Beers, Timothy C.","Benavides, B. Izamar T.","Bender, Chad F.","Bernardi, Mariangela","Bershady, Matthew","Beutler, Florian","Bidin, Christian Moni","Bird, Jonathan","Bizyaev, Dmitry","Blanc, Guillermo A.","Blanton, Michael R.","Boquien, Médéric","Borissova, Jura","Bovy, Jo","Brandt, W. N.","Brinkmann, Jonathan","Brownstein, Joel R.","Bundy, Kevin","Bureau, Martin","Burgasser, Adam","Burtin, Etienne","Cano-Díaz, Mariana","Capasso, Raffaella","Cappellari, Michele","Carrera, Ricardo","Chabanier, Solène","Chaplin, William","Chapman, Micha